        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_5e7d47_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_5e7d47",
        "thought_text": "Use a greedy approach where you take the first character of t as the first character of s, then skip the next n-1 characters (where n is the length of s) and take the next character as the second character of s, and so on. This approach leverages the fact that the length of the repeated segments corresponds to the position in the original string.",
